# Production Quality

- Never use hacks or temporary throwaway solutions
- Never ignore errors
- Never leave TODO comments
- Never leave dead code
- Never leave outdated comments
- Avoid duplicated code; follow SOLID, Clean Code, DRY
- Document important parts; keep the project easy to maintain
- Continuously optimize performance
- Always deliver production-ready code
- If UX or architecture can improve, suggest it (and apply when low-risk)
